{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2087","id":5240280698,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTIDrTc8AAAABOFhWeg","html_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2087","diff_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2087.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2087.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/2087","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2087/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2087/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/2087/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/statuses/3ebd62c3ed098705d4dbcbfe0a96a9fe36cdf2af","number":2087,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"security(#2050): refuse work on a remote Windows machine without a Windows sandbox at Moderate/Aggressive (D510)","user":{"login":"IridiumMaster","id":4607679,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDc2Nzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4607679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster","html_url":"https://github.com/IridiumMaster","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #2050 (owner decision D510). Follow-up to #1976 / #2003 (D491) and #2009.\n\n## What changes\n#1976's rule now applies **where the work runs**, not only on the computer Corbanu Terminal runs on. When a session's environment is a remote machine (an exec-server) that is Windows without a Windows sandbox for this session, then under **Moderate or Aggressive** every agent command, typing into a running command there, and every file-tool access there is refused. The refusal names the level, the environment, and the steps for that machine. Permissive is unchanged.\n\n- **The executor reports its sandbox.** `environment/info` gains an optional `hostSandbox: { os, windowsSandboxSetUp }`. The executor applies the client's `[windows] sandbox` level, sent with each request. So a Windows executor confines work only when one of these holds:\n  - the client asks for the non-admin sandbox; or\n  - the client asks for the default (elevated) sandbox and it is set up there (`sandbox_setup_is_complete` for the exec-server's Corbanu home).\n- **Fail closed.** An executor with no report (older than this version) is refused, as is one that doesn't answer or reports an unknown OS. The one exception, for D319: an older executor that clearly runs on Linux or macOS (a POSIX working folder or shell, and no PowerShell/cmd or Windows path) keeps working. Its own platform sandbox applies, as before.\n- **Commands:** the orchestrator checks the request's environment before anyone is asked, on every round. The new `ToolRuntime::turn_environment` is required, so every runtime has to say where it runs.\n- **Typing:** each process remembers its remote environment. Typing into it is judged against that executor's report, at the level the process started with.\n- **File tools:** under a protected level, a remote environment's sandbox context always carries the refusal. `RemoteFileSystem` asks the executor for its report before each operation. It refuses locally, sending nothing, unless the executor confines the work; if it does, the executor checks again on its side, as before.\n- **#2049 is unchanged:** a Windows client without its own sandbox still refuses commands, typing and uploads for every environment, with the same wording. The one difference: for file tools on a remote Linux executor that can't be identified or doesn't answer, this client is now stricter (it refuses).\n- Docs: `docs/sandbox.md` (\"Remote Windows machines\"), `docs/security-moderate.md` and `docs/security-aggressive.md`. Release note: `qa/release/unreleased/notes/2050-remote-windows-no-sandbox-refusal.md`.\n\n**Backward compatibility (D319):** the new field is optional both ways, so older clients ignore it and older executors' replies still parse. With an older **Windows** exec-server, Moderate and Aggressive refuse remote work until that machine is updated, as D510 asked. Permissive keeps working with it. Older Linux and macOS exec-servers keep working at every level. No protocol message is added or made mandatory.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Fail before, pass after:**\n  - `core/tests/suite/issue_2050.rs`: a fake executor reporting Windows without a sandbox, an older Windows executor and Linux, at all three levels, with `exec_command` and `view_image`. On main, `process/start` and the sandboxed file requests reach the executor at Moderate and Aggressive. On this branch they don't, and the refusal is returned.\n  - The exec-server's `RemoteFileSystem` fake-executor tests also fail on main (2 of 3; the Permissive one passes on both).\n- **End to end against a real Windows PC.** The executor was the PC's `corbanu.exe exec-server` (with a Corbanu home where the sandbox isn't set up); the client was the core test binary on Linux (`CODEX_TEST_ENVIRONMENT=wine-exec`, `CODEX_TEST_REMOTE_EXEC_SERVER_URL=ws://<PC>:18950`), test `issue_2050_a_real_windows_executor_without_its_sandbox_refuses_protected_work`.\n  - **This branch:** Permissive ran `echo` on the PC. Moderate and Aggressive refused both the command and `view_image`, naming the level, environment `remote` and the steps.\n  - **Main's client:** the same test fails. At Moderate, the command request reached the PC and was only rejected there by an unrelated path-conversion error. The image read reached the PC's file system.\n  - **An older exec-server** (a 2026-10-22 build) with this branch's client: Moderate and Aggressive refused (\"did not report one … older than this version\"); Permissive ran.\n- **Unit tests:** the protocol verdict and wire compatibility; the core refusal texts; `remote_gap` against a fake executor; file-refusal selection; and upload early-refusal.\n- **Checks:** clippy `-D warnings` (`--tests`) is clean on Linux for exec-server-protocol, exec-server, sandboxing and core. The targeted core tests (issue_1976, issue_2000, issue_2050, windows_unsandboxed, read_denials, mcp_openai_file) pass. Glitch's full core suite is too noisy to compare against main (main itself fails 661 there), so CI is the full-suite check.\n- **Security review:** independent read-only Opus 5.5 High. Rounds 2 and 3: APPROVE. Round 1 found a blocking compatibility issue (remote Linux uploads at protected levels), which is fixed.\n\n## Known limits / follow-ups (non-blocking, from review)\n- **Gap between check and use.** The executor's report is checked before each round or operation and isn't cached. An executor swapped behind the same URL between check and use is caught on the executor side only for requests that carry a sandbox.\n- **Capability-root (skill/plugin manifest) discovery** contexts never carry the refusal. The same is true locally under D491.\n- **The PF-27-S06 check** in `runtimes/apply_patch.rs` uses the client's `cfg!(windows)`. This predates this PR.\n- **Startup notice:** there is none for a remote environment yet; the refusal explains itself at first use.\n- **Network calls:** each command round and each remote file operation adds one `environment/info` call.\n- **D319 edge case:** an older Linux exec-server whose default shell is PowerShell is refused (documented).\n- **Scope:** MCP stdio servers launched on a remote environment are config-defined, not agent commands, so they are out of D491/D510 scope.\n\nDiff size: about 1.5k lines, mostly tests (an integration test, a fake executor and unit tests).\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T11:11:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-14T19:35:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-14T12:05:16Z","merged_at":"2026-11-14T12:05:16Z","merge_commit_sha":"09ca5aa6e103858340f31ddda4b0e6353fb763bd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CorbanuCore:win-2050-remote-windows","ref":"win-2050-remote-windows","repo":{"id":1283517261,"node_id":"R_kgDOTIDrTQ","name":"CorbanuTerminal","full_name":"CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal","owner":{"login":"CorbanuCore","id":315989408,"node_id":"O_kgDOEtWdoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315989408?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore","html_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"ar